   {
    "caption": "Zero watts… zero ice"
   },
   {
    "caption": "yet this clay jug cools water!"
   },
   {
    "caption": "How?"
   },
   {
    "caption": "Clay is full of tiny pores"
   },
   {
    "caption": "Water slowly seeps through them"
   },
   {
    "caption": "out onto the jug's surface"
   },
   {
    "caption": "Hot, dry air evaporates it"
   },
   {
    "caption": "and evaporation needs energy: heat"
   },
   {
    "caption": "It takes that heat from the water inside"
   },
   {
    "caption": "so the water cools, with no power"
   },
   {
    "caption": "The drier the air"
   },
   {
    "caption": "the more it evaporates, the more it cools"
   },
   {
    "caption": "In humid air? It barely works"
   },
   {
    "caption": "Your body uses the same trick"
   },
   {
    "caption": "when you sweat to cool down"
   },
   {
    "caption": "So the clay jug sweats, just like you"
   },
   {
    "caption": "to keep your water cold!"
   }
